\\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & -\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+(-2){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & -\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nOn the right-hand side, we obtain the change-of-coordinates matrix from $S$ to $B.$ Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n{P}_{S\\to B}=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ -1 & -\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}].\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124975 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124492 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6b973d79-8fe4-5033-8202-9693004855dc" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Change-of-Coordinates Matrix When One of the Bases is the Standard Basis"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "413babe6-bd06-53d8-b116-6f3c125d0b8f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321665} {:answer/id #uuid "437a9aba-29f6-58b7-9e94-335db5d38686" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -3 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321680} {:answer/id #uuid "5bbeaebe-5b9a-59b4-b02f-a834002d78a9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ -3 & -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321873} {:answer/id #uuid "5da43626-5807-5c19-9ce4-b9a4f29b4e29" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ -2 & -3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321886} {:answer/id #uuid "97341cc3-b696-5ed4-bcde-4f652a3e90a3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322354}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5da43626-5807-5c19-9ce4-b9a4f29b4e29" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ -2 & -3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321886} :answer-field/id #uuid "a89f17c1-0ec4-5bf7-9f2a-f1f548e39054" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323495}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b7561091-5a13-5f20-989c-89982f4b4b54" :question/math-academy-id "q-36366" :question/problem "Let $B={{b}_{1},{b}_{2}}$ be a basis of ${R}^{2}$ and let $S$ be the standard basis of ${R}^{2}.$ \nFind the change-of-coordinates matrix ${P}_{B\\to S}$ from $B$ to $S$ if \n\n$$\n{b}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}],\\,{b}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Recall  that the standard basis of ${R}^{2}$ consists of the vectors ${e}_{1}$ and ${e}_{2},$ given by\n\n$$\n{e}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,{e}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThe components of the vectors of $B$ are just the coordinates relative to the standard basis:\n\n$$\n[{b}_{1}]_{S}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}],\\,[{b}_{2}]_{S}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThe change-of-coordinates matrix from $B$ to $S$ is a matrix whose respective columns are the coordinates of the vectors of $B$ relative to the basis $S.$ \n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n{P}_{B\\to S}=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ -2 & -3\\end{aligned}].\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186416601 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124492 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6b973d79-8fe4-5033-8202-9693004855dc" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Change-of-Coordinates Matrix When One of the Bases is the Standard Basis"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "08510d9c-0008-5b50-b913-170c103ba9c1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498